# Go tooling compares files byte for byte: gofmt reports a CRLF file as
# unformatted, so on Windows -- where git defaults to core.autocrlf=true --
# `make lint` fails on files nobody has touched, and the only way to pass is
# to rewrite every file in the repository.
#
# Pinning the working-tree form settles it. Everything here is read by Linux
# tools in the end: the CNI plugin ships as a Linux binary, the shell scripts
# run in a container, and a CRLF in cni_ds_init would make its shebang fail
# with a message that does not mention line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so never translated and never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
